Good idea.  But, as I think has already been mentioned, monsters should
perhaps have another attribute associated with them - size.  Goblins are
small, bugbears are medium, umber hulks are large, and dragons are huge.
Of course, the distinction between size should be somewhat finer than 
this, but you get the general idea.  Then you can have little monsters
hiding behind big ones.  The possiblities are endless...

Back to silhouettes - I see no reason why it shouldn't work.  Although
it might be interesting to make it more difficult for the player to see
*exactly* how far the monster is - after all, depth perception is more
difficult when the light is poor.  Maybe you could displace the oncoming 
creature by one square either way?

